<!--Render Target Documentation — SourceMaps
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.SourceMaps-->
<rdoc:SourceMaps xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Source Map V3 beside each SCAD file
  </is>
  <documentation>
    The renderer writes a Source Map V3 file next to each SCAD output:

        Wall.scad
        Wall.scad.map

    The map records BML source file, line, and column for every generated SCAD
    line, so diagnostics can point at the BML position rather than the generated
    SCAD.

    Source Map V3 is the language-agnostic format (version 3, sources, mappings).
    Each generated SCAD line is one mappings group. This implementation points
    every line at the block definition's BML position. The map is the optional
    sourceMap field on the RenderOutput file. The host writes Wall.scad.map
    when that field is present.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:HelperFunctions" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:SourceMaps>
